Refs:
# Types:
#   feat     = new feature (minor version bump)
#   fix      = bug fix (patch version bump)
#   docs     = documentation only changes
#   perf     = performance improvement
#   refactor = code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   test     = adding or updating tests
#   chore    = maintenance, tooling, formatting, packaging
#   style    = formatting (spaces, lint, typos)
#----------------------------
# Scopes (Fontshow):
#   build      = build system / github
#   catalog    = catalog-specific logic (labels, sample rendering, LaTeX block generation)
#   ci         = CI / GitHub Actions
#   cli        = parser registration + CLI orchestration wrappers
#   config     = configuration files
#   core       = core pipeline, data flow, orchestration
#   decision   = formal decision (architecture, rules...)
#   dev        = development (tooling, hooks, scripts)
#   diagnostics = internal diagnostic in the pipeline
#   discovery  = interaction with installed fonts, fontconfig, fonttools
#   docs       = documentation (MkDocs, README, architecture)
#   dump       = dump_fonts tool
#   git        = git configuration
#   inventory  = schema/types/validation/building/parsing/inference of inventory JSON
#   latex      = generic LaTeX escaping, detokenize safety, NFSS id helpers
#   output     = output format
#   ontology   = data erlated to scripts aand languages
#   parser     = parse_font_inventory tool
#   planning   = planning and design documents
#   schema     = json schema definition and data validation
#   release    = versioning, tags, changelog
#   unicode    = charset decoding, Unicode blocks coverage, script coverage math
#   validation = validation tools
# ----------------------------
# Rules:
# - Subject line max 72 characters
# - Use imperative mood ("add", "fix", "document")
# - No trailing period
# - Body is optional but encouraged for non-trivial changes
#
# Breaking changes:
#   Add "!" after the type or include "BREAKING CHANGE:" in the body.
#
#   feat!(core): change inventory schema to v2.0
#
# Body (optional):
#   Explain WHY, not WHAT.
#
# Footer (optional):
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
# ----------------------------
# Body (optional):
# Explain *why* the change is made, not just *what*.
#
# ----------------------------
## Examples:
#   feat(core): add inventory validation option
#   docs(docs): document schema evolution rules
#   fix(catalog): handle missing family names gracefully
#   chore(core): convert Fontshow into a proper Python package
#
